  "raw": " catch up, some analysts believe the market share of others in the smartphone market is poised to get even bigger.\n\nAccording to a recent report by Strategy Analytics, a market share analysis firm based in London, Huawei's shipments fell 27% year-on-year in the second quarter, compared to 30% decline last year. Also, the company's market share slipped, from 7.3% to 5.4%, while others grabbed a bigger share by grabbing 1.5 percentage points, compared to 1.8 points.\n\nAlthough Huawei has been trying hard to make up for lost market share, industry insiders are saying the firm has a tough time with its new Huawei P9 and P9 Plus models, not to mention the company being targeted with massive U.S. government sanctions.\n\nThe firm has been scrambling to fix things with U.S. government to make sure the two models pass American National Telecommunications and Infrastructure Security Bureau (NTISB) as well as the Financial",
